# XB-Git-Commit and XB-Build-Date carry the build's identity.  The XB- prefix
# is Debian's own mechanism for adding a field to a binary package, so the
# field is correct and lintian simply has no name for it.  It goes beside the
# version rather than into it, because Version's only job is telling apt
# which of two packages is newer.
# See policies/packaging-and-release-model.md, "Identifying a build".
@PACKAGE@: unknown-field XB-Git-Commit
@PACKAGE@: unknown-field XB-Build-Date
